{"schema_version": 1, "run_id": "wave8-pr81b-system-hardening-lessons.xGF7Aw", "commit_range": "862842bcf..19bb5b2b5", "reporter": "security-guardian", "recorded_by": null, "source": "governance-agent", "reviewed_at_sha": "19bb5b2b5", "recorded_at": "2026-09-23T22:35:17+00:00", "pass_ordinal": 2, "finding_id": "G8-1s", "severity_native": "LOW", "severity_mapped": "BLOCKING", "trigger": "root/CAP_SYS_ADMIN in the agent mount namespace mounts an unresponsive FUSE or stale hard NFS filesystem at or below /proc/sys, then posture is re-dispatched", "impact": ["I5"], "exposure": ["E5", "E3"], "epistemic_status": "likely", "independent_reporters": 1, "policy_floor": null, "provenance": "introduced", "file": "agents/plugins/system_hardening/src/system_hardening_linux.cpp", "line": "9", "summary": "A hung filesystem still blocks open/statfs/read and can pin workers; no in-plugin bound can cancel a hung syscall. Comment narrowed and threat-model boundary documented in 3cd74d7ab. OPEN pending owner adjudication: out-of-threat-model (actor already root) vs platform per-command deadline issue.", "classification": "truth-contradiction", "classification_rationale": "code or doc disagrees with behaviour", "disposition": "open", "adjudicated_by": null, "adjudication_rationale": null, "caused_by": null, "waiver_rationale": null}
{"schema_version": 1, "run_id": "wave8-pr81b-system-hardening-lessons.xGF7Aw", "finding_id": "G8-1s", "recorded_by": "orchestrator", "recorded_at": "2026-09-25T09:40:26+00:00", "pass_ordinal": 0, "reviewed_at_sha": "19bb5b2b5", "commit_range": "862842bcf..19bb5b2b5", "disposition": "linked-to-#4875", "impact": ["I5"], "severity_mapped": "BLOCKING", "summary": "Owner ruling (2026-09-25): raise as a general issue. Tracked on the existing issue #4875 (agent file-reading plugins have no execution deadline, so a stalled mount pins a command-pool worker); evidence comment posted there. #4875 is an active (non-roadmap) issue.", "adjudicated_by": "repository owner direct instruction 2026-09-25; the owner is also the change author, so this is not an independent adjudication", "adjudication_rationale": "The hazard needs root or CAP_SYS_ADMIN in the agent mount namespace and cannot be bounded inside a plugin (a hung open/statfs/read cannot be cancelled); the fix is a platform-level per-command deadline and worker replacement, already tracked on #4875. The plugin narrows its own comment and documents the boundary."}
